{"id": "sfmta-garage-contracts-counted-by-fee", "title": "Muni’s garage contracts counted only the fee: $231 million spent before the Board saw them", "seconds": 128.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "30cd1c4717b1954a", "words": 385, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["sources", "established[0]"], "text": "February 2022. The Board’s analyst opens four of Muni’s garage contracts.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.94, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bla", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 2 February 2022", "text": "SFMTA garage management contracts, Files 22-0004 to 22-0007", "mark": "garage management"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.78, 1.85, 2.01, 2.31, 2.73, 3.07, 3.32, 3.42, 3.75, 4.15]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Since 2012, private operators have run 20 public garages for the agency.", "t0": 5.06, "t1": 9.53, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "20 public garages", "kicker": "Private operators", "sub": "a monthly fee, plus every cost reimbursed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.56, 1.26, 1.65, 2.14, 2.28, 2.5, 2.84, 3.17, 3.65, 3.78, 3.92]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Each gets a monthly fee, and all its costs reimbursed.", "t0": 9.65, "t1": 12.51, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "20 public garages", "kicker": "Private operators", "sub": "a monthly fee, plus every cost reimbursed"}, "emph": ["all its costs"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.46, 0.54, 0.9, 1.27, 1.47, 1.65, 1.83, 2.2]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "How much did the four contracts pay out, by January 2022?", "t0": 12.63, "t1": 16.93, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Four garage contracts", "sub": "February 2012 to January 2022"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.53, 0.65, 0.89, 1.41, 1.65, 2.2, 2.4, 2.93, 3.2]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "231,349,383 dollars.", "t0": 16.93, "t1": 19.89, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$231,349,383", "label": "paid out under four SFMTA garage contracts", "sub": "February 2012 to January 2022"}, "emph": ["231,349,383"], "wt": [0.04, 0.39, 0.62, 0.91, 1.53, 1.8, 2.13, 2.51]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "In December 2011, each garage-group contract was set at its fees alone:", "t0": 20.51, "t1": 25.37, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A, B and C garages", "kicker": "December 2011", "sub": "management fees only", "chip": "$907,920"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.57, 0.86, 1.48, 1.72, 2.39, 2.93, 3.07, 3.29, 3.38, 3.55, 3.89]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "907,920 dollars.", "t0": 25.37, "t1": 28.04, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A, B and C garages", "kicker": "December 2011", "sub": "management fees only", "chip": "$907,920"}, "emph": ["907,920"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.63, 0.96, 1.4, 1.64, 1.94, 2.26]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[1]"], "text": "The 5th and Mission Garage, 587,510. Reimbursed costs were left out.", "t0": 28.46, "t1": 34.78, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["5th and Mission Garage", "$587,510"], "b": ["the operators’ costs", "left out"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["left out"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.44, 0.55, 0.83, 1.69, 2.0, 2.27, 2.86, 3.28, 3.56, 3.82, 4.69, 5.29, 5.65, 5.81, 6.07]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "And of everything paid out, how much was fees?", "t0": 34.9, "t1": 38.13, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Of $231,349,383 paid out", "sub": "how much was fees?"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.39, 0.84, 1.13, 1.68, 1.92, 2.21, 2.41]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "4,578,205 dollars. The rest was reimbursed costs.", "t0": 38.13, "t1": 42.11, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$4,578,205", "label": "management fees, 2012 to January 2022", "sub": "the rest: reimbursed costs"}, "emph": ["4,578,205"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.67, 0.93, 1.19, 1.5, 2.33, 2.53, 2.8, 3.0, 3.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[1]"], "text": "Why does it matter? The Charter sends any contract of 10 million or more to the Board.", "t0": 42.53, "t1": 46.79, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charter section 9.118(b) sends any contract of $10 million or more to the Board of Supervisors.", "kicker": "The Board line"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.33, 0.44, 1.06, 1.22, 1.59, 1.87, 2.08, 2.58, 2.7, 2.94, 3.3, 3.43, 3.67, 3.77, 3.88]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Counting only the fee kept each contract under that line for ten years.", "t0": 46.91, "t1": 50.46, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charter section 9.118(b) sends any contract of $10 million or more to the Board of Supervisors.", "kicker": "The Board line"}, "emph": ["only the fee"], "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.58, 0.71, 1.03, 1.31, 1.52, 2.1, 2.31, 2.5, 2.78, 2.93, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Each contract’s spending passed 10 million dollars by fiscal 2014-15.", "t0": 50.68, "t1": 54.95, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2012-02-01", "to": "2022-02-25", "days": null, "fromLab": "contracts begin", "toLab": "first Board vote", "kicker": "Over the Board line"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.76, 1.18, 1.46, 1.68, 2.0, 2.34, 2.53, 2.92, 3.2, 3.68, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "So when did the Board of Supervisors first vote on them?", "t0": 55.07, "t1": 58.34, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2012-02-01", "to": "2022-02-25", "days": null, "fromLab": "contracts begin", "toLab": "first Board vote", "kicker": "Over the Board line"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.42, 0.56, 0.69, 0.93, 1.03, 1.76, 2.06, 2.3, 2.42]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "February 2022, retroactively.", "t0": 58.34, "t1": 60.81, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "25 February 2022", "label": "first Board vote, retroactive", "sub": "Resolutions 055-22 to 058-22"}, "emph": ["retroactively"], "wt": [0.04, 0.61, 0.89, 1.55]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "It came to the Board only because the agency asked to extend the contracts a year.", "t0": 61.23, "t1": 65.11, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "A one-year extension", "kicker": "January 2022", "sub": "the agency’s request to the Board"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.36, 0.46, 0.58, 0.87, 1.09, 1.39, 1.53, 1.99, 2.21, 2.37, 2.8, 2.91, 3.46, 3.55]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Why only the fee, in 2011? The agency and the City Attorney found no record explaining it.", "t0": 65.33, "t1": 70.88, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "SFMTA and City Attorney staff “were unable to locate records explaining why the contract amounts only referenced the management fees”.", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, footnote 7"}, "emph": ["no record"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.55, 0.71, 1.15, 1.34, 1.69, 2.59, 2.79, 3.21, 3.31, 3.42, 3.7, 4.11, 4.39, 4.6, 4.92, 5.45]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "The agency’s letter to the Board calls it a “regrettable error”.", "t0": 71.0, "t1": 74.07, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Staff recognizes this regrettable error", "kicker": "SFMTA letter, 21 January 2022"}, "emph": ["regrettable error"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.64, 0.9, 1.0, 1.13, 1.48, 1.8, 1.92, 2.01, 2.71]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The committee asked for a review of all its contracts, within 60 days.", "t0": 74.29, "t1": 77.96, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Review all SFMTA contracts", "kicker": "2 February 2022", "sub": "report within 60 days"}, "emph": ["all its contracts"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.55, 0.76, 0.89, 0.96, 1.28, 1.4, 1.57, 1.74, 2.49, 2.84, 3.22]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "A report dated September 2022 is listed on the file.", "t0": 78.08, "t1": 81.36, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "rpt", "kicker": "Attachment to Board File 220004", "text": "SFMTA Report 092822", "mark": "092822"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.54, 0.84, 1.35, 1.65, 2.21, 2.35, 2.68, 2.79, 2.9]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "What it found is not in the records we hold.", "t0": 81.48, "t1": 83.57, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "rpt", "kicker": "Attachment to Board File 220004", "text": "SFMTA Report 092822", "mark": "092822"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.3, 0.63, 0.79, 1.0, 1.09, 1.24, 1.6, 1.75]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[5]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "The agency’s own resolutions data skips the garage extensions of October 2021.", "t0": 83.69, "t1": 88.37, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "SFMTA Board resolutions", "kicker": "DataSF v5uc-gana", "sub": "the garage extensions of 5 October 2021: absent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.67, 0.87, 1.54, 1.85, 2.16, 2.27, 2.65, 3.2, 3.32, 3.77, 4.07]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The 2010 bid rules let no firm hold more than one garage group.", "t0": 88.59, "t1": 92.17, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "One group per firm", "sub": "2010 request for proposals"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Imperial Parking", "sub": "disqualified; senior partner of IMCO"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Pacific Park Management", "sub": "bought by Imperial, 2014"}], "kicker": "One-award rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.73, 1.0, 1.32, 1.57, 1.78, 2.1, 2.36, 2.53, 2.73, 2.93, 3.32]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Imperial Parking, IMCO’s senior partner, was disqualified on that ground.", "t0": 92.29, "t1": 96.57, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "One group per firm", "sub": "2010 request for proposals"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Imperial Parking", "sub": "disqualified; senior partner of IMCO"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Pacific Park Management", "sub": "bought by Imperial, 2014"}], "kicker": "One-award rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.59, 1.17, 1.71, 2.09, 2.63, 2.83, 3.59, 3.72, 3.9]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[4]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "In 2014, it bought Pacific Park Management, and took over Group A.", "t0": 96.69, "t1": 100.98, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A", "kicker": "2014", "sub": "assigned to Imperial Parking"}, "emph": ["Group A"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.49, 1.27, 1.44, 1.7, 2.15, 2.42, 3.05, 3.25, 3.51, 3.75, 4.09]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[8]"], "text": "Since February 2023, IMCO and LAZ manage all 21 garages and lots.", "t0": 101.1, "t1": 106.19, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["IMCO Parking", "$219 million"], "b": ["LAZ Parking", "$189 million"], "kicker": "All 21 garages and lots, since February 2023", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["all 21"], "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.74, 1.03, 1.92, 2.49, 2.69, 3.1, 3.42, 3.59, 4.08, 4.57, 4.69]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "The garages earn far more than they cost: 620 million dollars of revenue.", "t0": 106.41, "t1": 111.12, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["revenue to January 2022", "$620 million"], "b": ["spent", "$231 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["620 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.67, 0.91, 1.21, 1.42, 1.56, 1.72, 2.48, 2.76, 3.06, 3.41, 3.81, 4.16, 4.26]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "The question is ten years of spending with no Board vote.", "t0": 111.24, "t1": 113.71, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["revenue to January 2022", "$620 million"], "b": ["spent", "$231 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["no Board vote"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.5, 0.63, 0.84, 1.08, 1.17, 1.56, 1.74, 1.91, 2.2]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing here says any operator was paid for work not done.", "t0": 113.83, "t1": 116.76, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why only the fee was counted", "What the September 2022 report found", "That any operator was paid for costs it did not incur"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.53, 0.79, 1.02, 1.49, 1.65, 1.89, 2.06, 2.33, 2.58]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The September 2022 report, and the 2011 staff report.", "t0": 116.88, "t1": 122.39, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "SFMTA Report 092822: the review of all SFMTA contracts"}, {"who": "", "what": "The 2011 staff report that set the $907,920 amounts"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.34, 0.65, 1.23, 1.39, 1.89, 2.18, 2.68, 3.47, 3.72, 3.84, 4.07, 4.5, 4.86, 5.17]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has said why only the fee was counted.", "t0": 122.51, "t1": 125.08, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.69, 0.82, 1.06, 1.36, 1.61, 1.75, 1.97, 2.15]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 125.2, "t1": 127.31, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.63, 0.79, 1.03, 1.11, 1.21, 1.47, 1.75]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "Only the fee", "lead2": "Past the line", "lead3": "No record", "lead4": "The review", "lead5": "One rule, one owner", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "document"}